Each paragraph listed here is owed exactly one verdict:

- @!dyn.obligated-paragraphs!@

An identifier names a paragraph by the labels of its first and last sentences — `S3-S5` is the
paragraph whose sentences run from S3 through S5 — or by its one label where the paragraph holds a
single sentence. Copy each identifier exactly as it is listed; never count paragraphs yourself.

Judge each listed paragraph whole, and ask one question of it: is this paragraph all or part of a
result the document states?

- **Yes:** return a paragraph claim, with a `title:` line written as for a claim block. The claim
  covers the whole paragraph.
- **No** — it motivates, signposts, recaps or explains, and states no result: return a not-a-claim
  verdict, which carries the `paragraph:` line and nothing else.

A result that begins inside a listed paragraph — at any of its sentences — is recorded by that
paragraph's verdict, never by a claim block. Every listed paragraph gets one verdict, no paragraph
gets two, and a paragraph not listed gets none.

    @!paragraph-claim-open!@
    paragraph: <one identifier, copied from the list above>
    title: <one line naming the result>
    @!paragraph-claim-close!@
    @!paragraph-not-a-claim-open!@
    paragraph: <one identifier, copied from the list above>
    @!paragraph-not-a-claim-close!@